  "id": "COMPOUND:16431 - PROTEIN:3763",
  "verbalization": "Thiophene is implicated in the biological activity of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9 through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Thiophene directly targets CWR22R, which is then a target of multiple compounds, including aminophylline, Halocynthiaxanthin, and Brandisianin C. These compounds, in turn, target the same downstream protein, indicating a potential pathway where Thiophene may influence the activity of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9 through shared intermediates. The consistent presence of CWR22R as a common target across different compounds supports a mechanism where Thiophene may modulate the function of this protein via a common intermediate. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CWR22R as a central node in the interaction network, with Thiophene potentially acting as a modulator in this complex biological process.",
